Mr. Rowe,<br />
<br />
The staff's deficiency letter arising from examination 2011-0463 is attache=
d. It describes five deficiencies and asks the firm to describe the correct=
ive action it will take on each.<br />
<br />
Item 4 concerns custody. The staff's position is that Vandergrift Rowe's st=
anding authority to instruct client custodians to debit advisory fees from =
client accounts constitutes custody of client funds within the meaning of R=
ule 206(4)-2 under the Investment Advisers Act, that the firm was according=
ly required to obtain a surprise examination by an independent public accou=
ntant for calendar year 2010, and that no such examination was obtained and=
 no Form ADV-E was filed for that year.<br />
<br />
Please respond in writing within 30 days. As the letter states, the finding=
s described are based on the staff's examination and are not findings or co=
nclusions of the Commission.<br />
